  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>The gig economy in India is not one labour market, it is at least two very different ones sharing the same label.</strong>
    At one end sits platform-based delivery, mobility, and task work, where entry is fast and pay is tied closely to hours.
    At the other end sits freelance knowledge work, where entry takes longer to build but income has room to keep growing.
    Understanding which end of that spectrum a decision points toward matters more than reacting to gig-economy headlines. Picking the wrong end wastes years; picking the right one can put you on a path toward unlocking high income opportunities that a fixed-hours job usually cannot match.
  </p>

