      <li>The Code on Social Security, 2020 formally defines gig and platform workers and requires aggregators to fund a dedicated Social Security Fund, a real but partial safety net.</li>
      <li>Low-skill platform gig work has a fast entry and a hard pay ceiling; high-skill freelance work has a slower entry and a much higher ceiling.</li>
      <li>For long-term career planning, the useful question is which end of the spectrum a specific opportunity sits on, not whether "gig work" in general is good or bad.</li>
